# 🎯 Heart Stroke Prediction using Agentic AI — Interview Prep Guide

> **Your interview is in ~4 hours. Read this top to bottom. Every section has a 30-sec pitch, a 2-min detailed version, and likely follow-up questions.**

---

## 📌 SECTION 1: Project One-Liner (Memorize This)

> *"I built a multi-agent AI system for heart disease prediction that combines a KNN machine learning model with 6 specialized LLM agents — powered by Groq and Ollama — to provide not just a prediction score, but complete medical reasoning, lifestyle advice, downloadable PDF reports, and an interactive Q&A chatbot, all orchestrated through a single pipeline."*

---

## 📌 SECTION 2: Full Architecture Breakdown

### 🔄 End-to-End Pipeline Flow

```
User Input (Form or Free Text)
        │
        ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Helper Agent        │  ← Ollama (llama3:8b) — Extracts structured JSON from free text
│  (NLP Extraction)    │
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Prediction Agent    │  ← KNN Model + Scaler + One-Hot Encoding
│  (ML Inference)      │  → Returns: prediction (0/1) + risk %
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Reasoning Agent     │  ← Groq API (llama-3.3-70b-versatile)
│  (Medical Reasoning) │  → Explains WHY this risk level
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Lifestyle Agent     │  ← Groq API (llama-3.1-8b-instant)
│  (Health Advice)     │  → Diet, exercise, sleep, stress tips
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Report Agent        │  ← ReportLab (Python)
│  (PDF Generation)    │  → Professional downloadable report
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  History Manager     │  ← JSON persistence
│  (Save & Retrieve)   │  → Stores all past predictions
└────────┬────────────┘
         ▼
┌─────────────────────┐
│  Feedback Agent      │  ← Ollama (llama3.1:8b)
│  (Interactive Q&A)   │  → Follow-up medical questions
└─────────────────────┘
```

### **30-Second Version:**
> "My system uses a **pipeline orchestrator** ([pipeline.py](file:///e:/Heart_Stroke_Prediction/agents/pipeline.py)) that chains 6 agents sequentially. First, if the user types free text, the Helper Agent extracts structured medical features using a local LLM. Then the Prediction Agent runs KNN inference. The result feeds into a Reasoning Agent (Groq 70B) for medical interpretation, a Lifestyle Agent (Groq 8B) for health advice, and a Report Agent that generates a PDF. Everything is saved to history, and users can ask follow-up questions via the Feedback Agent."

### **2-Minute Detailed Version:**
> "The core problem I'm solving is that traditional ML models output a blind 0 or 1 — useless for a patient or a busy doctor who needs *context*. My system wraps a KNN classifier inside a multi-agent architecture where each agent has a specialized role.
>
> The **Helper Agent** runs locally via Ollama (llama3:8b). It takes unstructured text like 'I'm a 55-year-old male with chest pain and high cholesterol' and uses strict prompt engineering to output a clean JSON with exactly 11 required fields — Age, Sex, ChestPainType, RestingBP, Cholesterol, FastingBS, RestingECG, MaxHR, ExerciseAngina, Oldpeak, ST_Slope.
>
> The **Prediction Agent** loads 3 saved artifacts — [KNN_heart.pkl](file:///e:/Heart_Stroke_Prediction/KNN_heart.pkl), [scaler.pkl](file:///e:/Heart_Stroke_Prediction/scaler.pkl), [columns.pkl](file:///e:/Heart_Stroke_Prediction/columns.pkl). It manually one-hot encodes categorical features, applies MinMax scaling, and calls [predict()](file:///e:/Heart_Stroke_Prediction/app.py#20-76) and `predict_proba()` to get a binary prediction and a risk percentage.
>
> The **Reasoning Agent** uses Groq's API with `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` — a massive 70B parameter model — to generate a detailed medical interpretation of the results. Its system prompt strictly prevents diagnoses — it only explains risk factors.
>
> The **Lifestyle Agent** uses a smaller `llama-3.1-8b-instant` model via Groq because lifestyle advice doesn't need the depth of a 70B model. This is a conscious cost-optimization decision.
>
> The **Report Agent** uses Python's ReportLab to generate a professional A4 PDF with user details, health summary table, prediction, medical reasoning, lifestyle advice, and a legal disclaimer.
>
> Finally, the **Feedback Agent** runs locally via Ollama (llama3.1:8b) so the user can ask unlimited follow-up questions at zero API cost."

